// The Winsock model, for Prototype/Win32/check-winsock.sh. On Windows these
// declarations are the WinSock2 submodule of the WinSDK Clang module
// (stdlib/public/Platform/winsdk_um.modulemap: WinSock2.h, WS2tcpip.h,
// MSWSock.h and afunix.h, linking WS2_32.Lib). Clang won't add a submodule
// to WindowsModel's WinSDK from a second module map (its build of WinSDK
// reads only the map that defines it), so the model is a module of its own,
// which WinSDK+Winsock.swift re-exports from the WinSDK overlay model:
// `import WinSDK` and `WinSDK.socket` then work as on Windows. Code must
// never import WinSock2Model itself; check-winsock.sh fails if it does.
module WinSock2Model {
  header "winsock2.h"
  header "ws2tcpip.h"
  header "mswsock.h"
  export *
}
